;ZEsarUX configuration used by the `make run*` targets.
;
;Passed to the emulator as `--configfile`, so it replaces ~/.zesaruxrc
;entirely: project runs stay reproducible and never pick up (or clobber)
;the global config. Machine selection, Timex video and the tape file are
;still passed on the command line by the Makefile.
;
;Lines beginning with ; or # are ignored.

;Never write this file back on exit - it is version controlled.
--no-saveconf-on-exit

;Emulated joystick the game reads - do not change, src/input.c reads Kempston.
--joystickemulated "Kempston"

;Real (host) joystick mapping, copied from ~/.zesaruxrc. Everything below
;the sentinel is regenerated by `make zesarux-config`, so remap the pad in
;a normal ZEsarUX session (which saves to ~/.zesaruxrc) and then re-run
;that target - do not hand-edit below this point.
;--- BEGIN generated joystick mapping (make zesarux-config) ---
--joystickfirekey 0
--joystickfirekey2 -1
--joystickfirekey3 -1
--joystickfirekey4 -1
--realjoystickpath /dev/input/js0
--realjoystick-calibrate 16383
--steering-wheel-axis-number 0
--joystickevent -49 Up
--joystickevent +49 Down
--joystickevent -48 Left
--joystickevent +48 Right
--joystickevent 2 Fire
--joystickevent 1 Fire2
--joystickevent 5 Fire3
